      "content": "thanks. it feels a bit more real hearing that. it's just... i'm struggling to put it into words for the poem. i want to capture how self-destruction isn't just an end, but maybe the ultimate creative act. like, the moment you stop fighting the void and actually embrace it, you finally create something that can't be taken away or changed. do you see what i mean? that the act of letting go is the only way to make something truly honest?",
